---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Task Satiation vs. Aggregate Rebound in AI Demand"
  description="About: Task Satiation vs. Aggregate Rebound in AI Demand. Research paper in the OpenIE research catalog."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research paper · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Task Satiation vs. Aggregate Rebound in AI Demand
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Task-level satiation holds by definition: once a task completion predicate is true, more synthesis on that task buys nothing, and calls that undo it are harm. Aggregate satiation is a different claim. Cheaper synthesis opens new tasks and raises total use, as cheaper coal raised total coal use. The paper makes that rebound its central identification problem.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
      Hypotheses H1 (spend after completion) and H2 (Jevons in tasks) are stated with the data design that would identify them. No demand system or rebound estimate is reported. Capability scales. Appetite per task does not.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-laws">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion papers</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Research papers: <a href="/papers/agency/" class="text-brand-cyan">Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/gates/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metered Commit Gates</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="text-brand-cyan">Task Satiation vs. Aggregate Rebound</a>.
        Essay: <a href="/papers/spellcheck/" class="text-brand-cyan">Spell Check is Global</a>.
        Product white papers, kept apart: <a href="/products/mei/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metabolic Intelligence</a> · <a href="/products/jouleos/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Search for JouleOS</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/satiation/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/satiation.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/satiation/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Interactive figures
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
